<BaseLayout title="Diagrams and illustrations">
  <h1>Diagrams and illustrations</h1>
  <p>This index distinguishes Volvo owner-information illustrations from original conceptual drawings made for this reference. Conceptual drawings explain relationships or inspection zones; they are not OEM component-location, wiring, dimensional, exploded-parts or service diagrams.</p>

  <h2>Volvo factory / owner-information illustrations</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="../engine-compartment/">2021 S60 engine-compartment overview</a> — Volvo's labeled six-point service overview. Volvo notes that the arrangement varies by engine and model variant.</li>
    <li><a href="../fuses/">2021 S60 fuse locations and fuse-panel illustration</a> — Volvo's engine-compartment fuse image and market/equipment-qualified fuse tables.</li>
    <li><a href="../battery-electrical/">Support-battery reference</a> — Volvo owner-information image; read its source-year and support-battery caveat before using it to locate a battery.</li>
    <li><a href="../../interior/seats-controls/">Sensus centre-display views</a> — Volvo's display-interface illustration, not a photo of every trim's cabin equipment.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Original conceptual diagrams</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="../engine-and-drivetrain/">T5 / T6 / T8 powertrain map</a> — separate paths for T5 FWD, T5/T6 mechanical AWD and T8 electric rear drive.</li>
    <li><a href="../awd-system/">Mechanical AWD versus T8 eAWD</a> — compares functional power paths and makes clear that T8 does not use the mechanical rear propeller-shaft path.</li>
    <li><a href="../suspension-steering/">Suspension inspection map</a> — plan-view inspection zones for front steering/suspension and rear links; not exact component geometry.</li>
    <li><a href="../../repairs/brake-assembly/">Disc-brake cutaway</a> — labels rotor, pads, caliper, piston, carrier and hose in a generic cross-section; not S60-specific geometry.</li>
    <li><a href="../../troubleshooting/diagnostic-workflow/">Diagnostic workflow</a> — evidence-first sequence from symptom recording to repair verification.</li>
    <li><a href="../../maintenance/oil-level/">Electronic oil-level check sequence</a> — summarizes Volvo's measurement conditions; follow the installed software/manual.</li>
    <li><a href="../../maintenance/tires-wheels/">TPMS warning symbol</a> — simplified symbol reference, not an instrument-cluster screenshot.</li>
    <li><a href="../../repairs/paint-scratches/">Paint-layer damage diagram</a> — conceptual cross-section showing clear coat, base coat, primer and substrate.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Parts-catalogue drawings</h2>
  <p>For actual 2021 S60 brake component illustrations, use a VIN-filtered Volvo parts lookup. A secondary retailer's <a href="https://www.volvopartscounter.com/v-2021-volvo-s60--t5-inscription--2-0l-l4-gas/brakes--brake-components">2021 S60 T5 Inscription brake-components catalogue</a> shows that rotor, pad and carrier applications vary across trims and brake packages. It is a lookup aid, not a substitute for confirming the exact vehicle by VIN.</p>

  <h2>Visual quality rules</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Every photo must show the S60 or the exact subject named in its caption. Generic stock photos are not used to imply S60 fitment.</li>
    <li>Every vehicle photo identifies its model year/trim when known and calls out meaningful differences such as right-hand drive or market-specific equipment.</li>
    <li>Every factory illustration links to its Volvo source and preserves the source's model-year and variant caveats.</li>
    <li>Every original drawing is labeled conceptual and explains what it does not establish.</li>
    <li>Do not use a decorative image merely to fill space. If a relevant image cannot be sourced, a clear text explanation is better.</li>
  </ul>
</BaseLayout>
